      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the first six prime numbers.\n2. Calculate the sum of the first five primes.\n3. Divide the sum by the sixth prime and find the remainder.\n\nThe first six prime numbers are: \\(2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13\\).\n\nStep 1: The first five primes are \\(2, 3, 5, 7, 11\\). Their sum is:\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 = 28\n\\]\n\nStep 2: The sixth prime is \\(13\\). \n\nStep 3: We need to find the remainder when \\(28\\) is divided by \\(13\\). Let's perform the division:\n\\[\n28 \\div 13 \\approx 2.153846\n\\]\nSince we are concerned with the remainder, we only need the integer part of the quotient, which is \\(2\\). Now calculate the remainder:\n\\[\n28 - (13 \\times 2) = 28 - 26 = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the remainder when \\(28\\) is divided by \\(13\\) is \\(2\\).\n\nThe solution is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
