      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the first five primes.\n2. Identify the sixth prime.\n3. Find the sum of the first five primes.\n4. Divide this sum by the sixth prime.\n5. Find the remainder of this division.\n\n### Step 1: Identify the first five primes\nThe first five prime numbers are:\n\\[ 2, 3, 5, 7, 11 \\]\n\n### Step 2: Identify the sixth prime\nThe six prime numbers are:\n\\[ 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13 \\]\nSo, the sixth prime is:\n\\[ 13 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Find the sum of the first five primes\nCalculate the sum:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 + 3 + 5 + 7 &= 17, \\\\\n17 + 11 &= 28, \\\\\n28 + 13 &= 41\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nSo, the sum of the first five primes is:\n\\[ 41 \\]\n\n### Step 4: Divide the sum by the sixth prime and find the remainder\nWe need to find the remainder when 41 is divided by 13. This can be done using the modulo operation:\n\\[\n41 \\mod 13\n\\]\n\nTo perform this, we can use long division or a simple calculation:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n41 \\div 13 &\\approx 3.15 \\\\\n41 - 13 \\times 3 &\\approx 41 - 39 \\\\\n41 - 39 = 2 \n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nHence,\n\\[\n41 \\mod 13 = 2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
