      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum of the first five prime numbers is divided by the sixth prime number, let's proceed step by step.\n\n1. Identify the first six prime numbers:\n   - The first prime number is \\(2\\).\n   - The second prime number is \\(3\\).\n   - The third prime number is \\(5\\).\n   - The fourth prime number is \\(7\\).\n   - The fifth prime number is \\(11\\).\n   - The sixth prime number is \\(13\\).\n\n2. Calculate the sum of the first five prime numbers:\n   \\[\n   2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11\n   \\]\n\n3. Perform the addition step by step:\n   - Add \\(2\\) and \\(3\\):\n     \\[\n     2 + 3 = 5\n     \\]\n   - Add \\(5\\) to the result:\n     \\[\n     5 + 5 = 10\n     \\]\n   - Add \\(11\\) to the result:\n     \\[\n     10 + 11 = 21\n     \\]\n\n4. The sum of the first five prime numbers is \\(21\\).\n\n5. Now, need to find the remainder when \\(21\\) is divided by \\(13\\).\n\n6. Conduct the division:\n   \\[\n   21 \\div 13\n   \\]\n   Since \\(21\\) divided by \\(13\\) goes \\(1\\) time with a remainder, the division is:\n   \\[\n   21 = 13 \\times 1 + 8\n   \\]\n\n7. The remainder when \\(21\\) is divided by \\(13\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{8}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the remainder when the sum of the first five prime numbers is divided by the sixth prime number is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
